  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 4♥. West's spade opening lead is won with dummy's ♠A. South, hoping to avoid a trump loser, should finesse in hearts at trick 2. The finesse wins and South should cross to dummy to finesse again.\n\nWhen West discards, South cannot directly pick up East's hearts. South still can succeed with the help of a trump coup. South should cross to the dummy and play a spade from dummy, ruffing in hand.\n\nDummy still has an entry remaining to take another spade ruff. South's trump length has been reduced to that of East. South can exit in either diamonds or clubs. The defense will be unable to stop South from scoring tricks with both of his remaining hearts.",
